{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Lane f041: Gerrit 3052 patch set 1 (1bd22b89edc6) had Verified green on every job (CI run 39263070476) but LLM-Review -1 with 6 blocking findings, all valid. Patch set 2 (26b63fb0efbe) fixes them:\n(1, 2) templates/rebar-usage.md and its byte-synced region in templates/AGENTS.md taught tag/untag, session-logs, clarity-check/check-ac/quality-check. They are copied into new repos, so the hard cutover broke them now; they teach the new spellings.\n(3) docs/output-schemas.md listed the removed verbs as live commands and schema rows; it now names the new spellings against the same schemas.\n(4) docs/exit-codes.md, a file this change already edits, contradicted itself: it said session-logs was removed while its option-syntax and gate-convention prose still used it, clarity-check/check-ac/quality-check, exists and format. All rewritten.\n(5) show --field=<unknown> printed a silent null with exit 0. It now exits 2 with 'unknown --field', which is safe because file_impact and verify_commands are always present in state (empty list when unset).\n(6) _confirm.py docstring no longer lists tag/untag.\nAlso added test_show_field_reads_one_field_and_rejects_bad_combinations, covering --field happy path, unknown name and --output llm, which the reviewer noted was untested.\nThis overlaps story scabby-loverless-pipit (docs) for templates/ and docs/output-schemas.md; that story's plan should drop those edits. 274 related tests pass, lint is green, and the generators pass --check."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792419212985886001,"uuid":"4ac48372-cb06-474a-84d9-01833d40fe6b"}